    "explanation": "Both accounts are largely consistent with the record, and the arithmetic decides this case.\n\nFor the rider: I accept that you were in the terminal and did not see the messages. The platform's own chat log shows the system arrival notice and both driver messages were delivered with read_at null, and no in-app call was made, so your silence cannot be read as a refusal to coordinate. But POL-NS-04, the clause that would exonerate you, requires YOU to have sent a locating or coordinating message during the waiting window (limb (a)); the chat log holds no rider message at all, so the clause cannot run. Limb (c), whether your device was within the 200 m airport radius, is undecidable on this record: all 88 rider fixes report 45 to 80 m accuracy and are filtered out under the 25 m test, which POL-NS-04(c) makes neutral, evidence of neither presence nor absence. An undecidable limb does not exonerate you where limb (a) has already failed, and no adverse finding is built on fixes the policy discards. Your concession on the dwell arithmetic is correct and POL-NS-06 accordingly gives you nothing: there is no shortfall.\n\nFor the driver: the record supports the fee. POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs. The trip record carries your 'arrived' event at 23:13:10; the GPS trace places you inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius from 23:12:45, 25 seconds earlier; you held a single unbroken in-geofence run of 620 seconds against the 480-second AIRPORT minimum; and you terminated with RIDER_NO_SHOW at 23:23:20, after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. POL-NS-05 (false arrival) is not engaged, because at the arrived timestamp you were stationary inside the geofence, not moving and not beyond 300 m. POL-NS-06 (shortfall) is not engaged. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because your entire hold was inside the arrival radius, closest approach 22.4 m, so this is not a wrong-entrance case. The SGD 6.00 fee therefore stands as charged and reconciles with the fee schedule: the greater of the SGD 6.00 AIRPORT zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, with no defect under POL-NS-08(d).\n\nOn evidence weight: two artifacts are impaired at the schema level and are named here as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. EV-CHAT-00202 carries weight 0.85 on issue UNREAD_MESSAGE, and EV-DPROF-00202 carries weight 0.9 on issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH. Neither carries the deciding fact, the dwell and arrival being carried by EV-GPS-00202 and EV-TRIP-00202, both at weight 1.0. Neither is impaired under the policy limbs of POL-NS-08: there is no clock skew (the arrived event is 25 seconds from the nearest fix and the termination times agree), no trace gap (gaps empty, 116 fixes), no chat defect (message count matches trip_record.chat_message_count and the msg_id sequence 001 to 003 is unbroken), and no fare defect. EV-ADVIS-00202-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and can carry no fact; it is not needed, because the dwell was one continuous interval.\n\nThe compensation the driver is owed therefore stands. The anti-farming check does not trip: 1 no-show termination in the trailing 30 days is below the 4 required, and 1/168 = 0.006 is far below 0.08. The driver is paid 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 fee, SGD 4.80, under POL-NS-07. This is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling, on which amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd, and the rider's SGD 6.00 charge stands. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee, and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires.\n\nBecause the driver profile (weight 0.9) carries the anti-farming determination the compensation rests on, my confidence is capped at 0.90, still above the 0.70 escalation floor. The case does not escalate, and no clause produces a referral."
